From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: quire <quire@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:08:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] embed: documents

Cards: a host page can embed its own documents in a board. A card is a
rectangle whose box carries the new optional field `embed` ({"item"}),
read leniently (a value that is not an object with a string `item` loads
as a plain box), so the native format stays version 2 and a board written
by another program always opens. `BoxObj::is_embed` is the one test.

When the board is hosted (feature `embed`), src/embed_cards.rs:
- reports the cards of the current page, the camera and the engine's own
  interface over the canvas after every frame in which any of it changed
  (`onEmbedLayout`, at most once per frame, not from a discarded pass; a
  page without cards reports no pan or zoom);
- opens a card's document in the host (`onEmbedOpen`) instead of editing
  its label, on every path into label editing (double-click with its point,
  Enter, the menu's "Edit text"), and never in a read-only host;
- keeps the card the host edits (`setEmbedEditing`): no handles, no keys,
  no style panel, and the first primary or secondary press in the board or
  the board taking the focus ends it (`onEmbedEditEnd`), a primary press
  doing nothing else on the canvas; the middle button still pans, and the
  focus its press brings does not end it; a card that leaves the page or a
  new board end it as `gone`;
- inserts cards (`insertEmbed`: 480 x 360 by default, the first visible
  unlocked layer, one undo step, null when read-only) and shows the
  documents' live titles as the labels in place (`setEmbedTitles`: no undo
  step, no revision, again after every revision change);
- gives a single card no rotation handle, and a selection of cards alone
  no text settings in the style panel (their label is only the title);
- reports the documents of the cards on the clipboard (`clipboard` in the
  layout: a cut or copied card can still be pasted, so the host keeps its
  document).

The canvas reads the wheel's Shift and Alt from the wheel event itself: a
web page learns the other modifiers from key events on its canvas, which
it does not get while the host page has the keyboard focus.

Not hosted, a card is a plain rectangle. No new text is shown, so no
translation is added. Native tests in src/tests_embed.rs.
